# CODEX.md

## Purpose

Reusable SSH and debugging runbook for this Terraform-based OpenClaw deployment.

## Security Notes

- Do not store secrets in this file.
- Never commit `terraform.tfvars`, `*.tfstate`, or real tokens/keys.
- Treat Terraform outputs that include `gateway_token` or `#token=` URLs as sensitive.

## SSH Access

- Preferred wrapper: `bin/cloud-claw-ssh`
- Run remote command: `bin/cloud-claw-ssh -- <command>`
- Tail bootstrap log: `bin/cloud-claw-ssh -- tail -f /var/log/openclaw-bootstrap.log`
- Clean stale local SSH client sessions: `bin/cloud-claw-ssh-clean`

Useful Terraform outputs:

```bash
terraform output -raw repo_ssh_command
terraform output -raw ssh_command
terraform output -raw bootstrap_log_command
terraform output -raw repo_bootstrap_log_command
```

## Remote Paths

- App root: `/opt/openclaw`
- Compose file: `/opt/openclaw/docker-compose.yml`
- Env file: `/opt/openclaw/.env`
- Data/config volume: `/opt/openclaw/data`
- Workspace volume: `/opt/openclaw/workspace`
- Bootstrap log: `/var/log/openclaw-bootstrap.log`

## Discover Runtime Container Names

```bash
bin/cloud-claw-ssh -- sudo docker ps --format 'table {{.Names}}\t{{.Status}}\t{{.Ports}}'
```

Typical names are `openclaw-openclaw-1` and `openclaw-tailscale-1`, but always verify with `docker ps`.

## Fast Health Checks

```bash
# systemd + containers
bin/cloud-claw-ssh -- sudo systemctl status --no-pager openclaw
bin/cloud-claw-ssh -- sudo docker ps --format 'table {{.Names}}\t{{.Status}}\t{{.Ports}}'

# gateway port on VM
bin/cloud-claw-ssh -- curl -sv --max-time 5 http://127.0.0.1:18789/ 2>&1 | sed -n '1,40p'

# app container health/logs (replace <app_container>)
bin/cloud-claw-ssh -- sudo docker exec <app_container> openclaw health --json
bin/cloud-claw-ssh -- sudo docker inspect --format 'status={{.State.Status}} health={{if .State.Health}}{{.State.Health.Status}}{{else}}none{{end}} restartCount={{.RestartCount}} started={{.State.StartedAt}}' <app_container>
bin/cloud-claw-ssh -- sudo docker logs --since 20m <app_container> | tail -n 200
```

## Tailscale + URL Debug

```bash
# tailscale status (replace <tailscale_container>)
bin/cloud-claw-ssh -- sudo docker exec <tailscale_container> tailscale --socket=/tmp/tailscaled.sock status --json | jq -r '.Self.Online, .Self.DNSName, (.Health[]? // empty)'

# serve config and target
bin/cloud-claw-ssh -- sudo docker exec <tailscale_container> tailscale --socket=/tmp/tailscaled.sock serve status
bin/cloud-claw-ssh -- sudo docker exec <tailscale_container> sh -lc 'wget -S -O /dev/null -T 5 http://127.0.0.1:18789 2>&1 | sed -n "1,40p"'
```

Expected secure pattern:

- `OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_BIND=loopback`
- Tailscale sidecar uses `network_mode: "service:openclaw"`
- `tailscale serve` forwards to `127.0.0.1:18789`

## Recovery Commands

```bash
# restart full stack
bin/cloud-claw-ssh -- sudo systemctl restart openclaw

# restart tailscale sidecar only (replace <tailscale_container>)
bin/cloud-claw-ssh -- sudo docker restart <tailscale_container>

# watchdog timer (if enabled in bootstrap)
bin/cloud-claw-ssh -- systemctl status --no-pager openclaw-tailscale-watchdog.timer
```

## Common Failure Signatures

- `ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED` on tailnet URL:
  - OpenClaw not listening on `127.0.0.1:18789`, or Tailscale sidecar/serve not healthy.
- `origin not allowed` in Control UI:
  - `gateway.controlUi.allowedOrigins` is missing the dashboard origin.
- `unauthorized: gateway token missing`:
  - Use `dashboard_url_with_token_import` from Terraform output.
- `pairing required`:
  - Run `repo_pair_latest_command` (or `pair_latest_command`) from Terraform output.

## Manual Device Approval (Laptop Pairing)

```bash
# list pending pairing requests
bin/cloud-claw-ssh -- sudo docker exec openclaw-openclaw-1 openclaw devices list

# approve a specific request from the "Request" column
bin/cloud-claw-ssh -- sudo docker exec openclaw-openclaw-1 openclaw devices approve <requestId>
```

If you are already inside the OpenClaw container shell, run:
`openclaw devices list` and `openclaw devices approve <requestId>`.
After approving, run `openclaw devices list` again and confirm there are no pending requests.
Verified on March 11, 2026.
